        "guards"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "bonogo",
        "caelynn",
        "thalia",
        "wolf",
        "guards",
        "ephanna"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "bonogo": "evidence_gap",
        "caelynn": "evidence_gap",
        "thalia": "hit",
        "wolf": "hit",
        "guards": "hit",
        "ephanna": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The chamber fight includes the Players, the Wolf, Thalia, and multiple Guards (including elite/corrupted ones); council members are not explicitly confirmed present in the projection.\n\nBased on OBSERVED and CANON facts:\n\n- **Players (group)**: Present and actively engaged; they \u201crecount their story to the council\u201d and are in the chamber during the confrontation.\n- **the Wolf**: Explicitly in the **Council Room** and the central adversary of the fight.\n- **Thalia (Commander of the Guard)**: Present, with \u201cWolf is standing at Thalia\u2019s shoulder,\u201d and she actively participates (including attacking under the Wolf\u2019s influence).\n- **Guards**: Present in force\u2014some already positioned (\u201cring along the wall\u201d) and others \u201cbeing drawn here as reinforcements,\u201d including elite and corrupted guards who engage in combat.\n\nNotably **uncertain/absent**:\n- **Council members** are referenced indirectly (players addressing them), but there is no explicit confirmation they remain in the chamber during the fight.\n\nConflict note:\n- The Wolf\u2019s physical condition includes \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body,\u201d but also \u201cInvisible\u201d and escaping behaviors. These are conflicting OBSERVED states; the decapitation represents a terminal outcome, but the presence of escape/invisibility suggests that outcome may occur later or in a different moment of the encounter sequence.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Demographics: 6 Players; ~8 guards + 2 elite guards (some corrupted)\n- Geography: Large circular chamber, central table, hidden trapdoor\n- Defenses: Illusory walls, magical wards, rune activations\n- Atmosphere: Fireball-lit, tense, disheveled, high-stakes combat zone",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
