      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards on the council, and he views the cult as a dangerous perversion of magic that must be aggressively detected and contained using arcane means.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (Wizard\u2019s College) is the council\u2019s arcane representative. (OBSERVED/CANON)\n\nHis angle on the cult is strongly interventionist and magic-focused:\n- He sees the corrupted meat and the cult\u2019s influence as a \u201cperversion of magic\u201d and takes it very seriously. (CANON)\n- He is pushing for magical solutions, including a rune-based detection system and broader Wizard\u2019s College resources to locate and counteract the cult. (OBSERVED)\n- He is planning a magical lockdown of the city to contain the threat. (OBSERVED)\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Faction: Wizard\u2019s College (CANON)\n- Role/Title: Headmaster; representative of the arcane on the council (OBSERVED)\n- Goals: Deploy detection magic, lead anti-cult efforts, initiate lockdown (OBSERVED)\n- Attitude toward cult: Sees it as corrupt, dangerous magic that must be rooted out (CANON)\n- Approach: Proactive, arcane-heavy containment and detection strategy (OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
