      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead \u2014 specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Earlier escape/invisibility occurs, but the terminal outcome overrides it.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**:\n- He **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and was **\u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible; escapes\u201d**, suggesting a successful flee.\n- However, a later OBSERVED physical condition states **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n\nBecause \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d is a terminal outcome, it represents the final, authoritative state. The escape attempt happened during the fight, but it did not ultimately succeed.\n\nSo at fight\u2019s end: the Wolf is not at large\u2014he is dead.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** (terminal)\n- Prior state: Invisible, attempting escape via secret passage\n- Role: Central adversary in the council chamber battle\n- Alignment: Cultist, saboteur within Mirathorn\u2019s leadership",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
