      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence in the projection that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her attack is tied to **the Wolf\u2019s influence/order**, not confirmed corruption.\n\nFrom the available facts:\n- **Guards (OBSERVED)**: Corruption is clearly marked by \u201c**an oily sheen to their eyes**\u201d and ties to corrupted meat and cult activity.\n- **The Wolf (OBSERVED)**: Also shows corruption markers (\u201c**oily sheen to his eyes**\u201d) and actively **orders Thalia to attack the group**.\n\nThere is **no explicit mention of Thalia having corruption indicators** (like the oily sheen) or being affected by the same mechanics as the guards.\n\nGiven that, Thalia\u2019s behavior in the fight is best explained as:\n- Acting under **direct influence, manipulation, or command from the Wolf (OBSERVED)**  \n- Not confirmed to be physically or magically corrupted in the same way as the guards\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards corruption: oily sheen, linked to tainted meat (OBSERVED/CANON)\n- Wolf influence: issues commands, is himself corrupted (OBSERVED)\n- Thalia: no recorded corruption markers (absence in projection)\n\nIf you want to differentiate at the table: treat Thalia as **controlled or coerced**, not transformed\u2014unless you decide to extend the corruption later.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
