      "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber itself fights back with **arcane traps (force bursts + paralysis), debris hazards, and illusion effects**, especially targeting anyone without amulets.\n\nThe room\u2019s defenses are active and hostile:\n\n- **Arcane trap bursts (CANON + OBSERVED)**: These trigger against intruders (especially anyone without amulets), dealing **2d6 force damage** and potentially **temporarily paralyzing** targets. Guards are **exempt via amulets**.\n- **Targeting logic (CANON)**: \u201cIf players do not have the amulets, traps may target them,\u201d meaning the room discriminates friend vs. foe.\n- **Falling debris (OBSERVED)**: Environmental hazards force players to **dodge falling debris**, adding chaos and positional pressure.\n- **Illusion effects (CANON)**: Players are already noted as **disoriented by illusory walls/illusion spells**, so the room can distort positioning, sightlines, or paths mid-fight.\n- **Rune alarms (OBSERVED)**: These escalate the situation by alerting defenders and increasing pressure during combat.\n- **Ambient tell (CANON)**: The **wall hum changes** when something significant happens\u2014subtle cue that traps or effects are activating.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps (force + paralysis), amulet-based targeting\n- Terrain hazards: Falling debris\n- Magical effects: Illusions causing disorientation\n- Systems: Rune alarms, reactive wall-hum signaling",
      "embedding_similarity": null
