      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia is very likely compromised\u2014The Wolf is actively influencing her and has already ordered her to attack the group, so something is definitely off.\n\nBased on OBSERVED facts, The Wolf is physically close\u2014\u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d\u2014during the council events. He is a confirmed cultist, saboteur, and manipulator who \u201cattempts to deceive the council\u201d and \u201csteer discussion in the wrong direction.\u201d Crucially, he has already \u201corders Thalia to attack the group,\u201d indicating direct influence or control over her actions.\n\nThere\u2019s no CANON or OBSERVED evidence confirming Thalia\u2019s independent loyalty or resistance. Combined with The Wolf\u2019s corrupting influence and proximity, this strongly suggests she may be compromised, coerced, or under manipulation rather than acting freely.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Influence: The Wolf (cultist, deceiver) is at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\n- Behavior Trigger: The Wolf has ordered Thalia to attack the party\n- Context: Active council sabotage and deception in progress\n- Risk Level: High\u2014likely compromised or under external control\n\nConclusion: Treat Thalia as unreliable in this meeting unless proven otherwise.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_4_v2",
      "question": "If the council keeps talking and doesn't act, what bites us?",
