      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is tense and disturbed\u2014guards are visibly compromised, the aftermath of illusion and chaos lingers, and the Wolf\u2019s fate is unmistakable: \"Decapitated; head removed from body.\"\n\nWhat you should emphasize:\n\n- The body of **the Wolf (actor)** is no longer whole\u2014\"Decapitated; head removed from body\"\u2014with clear signs he took heavy damage before that moment.\n- Several **Guards (other)** show corruption: an **\u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d** is noticeable on all checked guards, creating immediate paranoia about who is still trustworthy.\n- The room still carries the **aftermath of illusion magic** (CANON): players may recall confusion, duplicate Wolves, or lingering uncertainty about what was real.\n- Guards are **tense, disorganized, and reacting** (OBSERVED), suggesting the fight destabilized security in a critical political space.\n- The presence or implication of a **secret passage beneath/near the chamber** (OBSERVED from Wolf goals) becomes more relevant in hindsight\u2014this was an escape route.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Illusion magic recently used (Wolf duplicates)\n- Inhabitants: Corrupted guards (oily sheen), tense survivors\n- Notable Features: Council chamber, hidden/secret passage access\n- Atmosphere: Paranoia, instability, political tension after violence",
