      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room was heavily disrupted\u2014**almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball**, its magical defenses activated (runes and illusory walls), and it\u2019s now **disheveled** from the conflict.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled (OBSERVED)\n- Atmosphere Changes: almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball (OBSERVED); air thick with anticipation turned into active combat chaos\n- Defenses Activated: runes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell; illusory walls in play; ancient wards influencing the battlefield (OBSERVED)\n- Geography Impact: large circular room with central table remained, but battlefield hazards (illusory walls, trapdoor presence) became tactically relevant rather than just architectural (OBSERVED)\n\nIn short, Session 12 transformed the chamber from a formal deliberation space into an active, magically volatile battlefield, with visible fire damage/disruption and triggered defenses altering how the room functions.",
