      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead \u2014 **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** \u2014 and there\u2019s no evidence his corruption was cured before death.\n\nThe OBSERVED record shows conflicting states (escaping while invisible vs. being killed), but the terminal outcome takes precedence: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Additionally, Bonogo\u2019s role explicitly includes \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d reinforcing that this is the final state at end of Session 12.\n\nRegarding corruption: the Wolf had \u201can oily sheen to his eyes,\u201d indicating active corruption, and there is no OBSERVED resolution (no cleansing or recovery). So he died while still corrupted.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d; oily sheen to his eyes; took major damage**\n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): Previously escaping/invisible, but superseded by death\n- Mental State (OBSERVED): Desperate, begging for release or death\n- Faction (OBSERVED): Cultist\n- Role (CANON): Central adversary in the council chamber conflict\n\nConclusion: Dead, body mutilated, corruption unresolved at time of death.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
