      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active saboteur manipulating the council with illusions and deception; after, he\u2019s a broken, desperate figure who ends up **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d** and no longer a strategic threat.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **second-in-command** guard and **cultist/sympathizer** working to **sabotage council decision-making**.\n- He actively deceives: using **Deception/Persuasion**, creating **illusory duplicates**, and **steering discussions**.\n- Operationally, he\u2019s evasive and tactical: **Invisibility**, escape routes, and coordinated disruption.\n- Mentally, he\u2019s controlled but dangerous\u2014focused on misdirection and escape.\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- His state collapses: **desperate**, **begging for someone to release him**, even **begging to be killed**, with **regret**.\n- Physically and narratively resolved: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d**\n- Prior corruption is visible: **\u201coily sheen to his eyes.\u201d**\n- He shifts from mastermind to **defeated victim of the conflict**, no longer acting or influencing events.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Saboteur \u2192 Defeated enemy\n- Mental State: Controlled/deceptive \u2192 Desperate/regretful\n- Physical Condition: Active/invisible \u2192 **Decapitated**\n- Tactics: Illusions, deception \u2192 None (terminated)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_thalia",
      "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
