      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was not corrupted\u2014she was ensorcelled and manipulated by the Wolf, who used her position to influence events.\n\nThalia\u2019s state is clearly **ensnarement, not corruption**. She is explicitly noted as **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d** and even **\u201censorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d** (OBSERVED, Thalia physical_condition). Crucially, she **\u201cdoes not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d**, which is a consistent marker of corruption seen in others like the guards and the Wolf himself (OBSERVED). Her mental state includes **\u201cInnocent\u201d** and that her **\u201cCharmed status ended\u201d**, after which she **\u201crealizes how dire the situation truly is\u201d**\u2014supporting that her actions weren\u2019t fully her own.\n\nThe Wolf\u2019s role ties directly into this: he **\u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d** and is associated with deception and manipulation (OBSERVED goals, CANON portrayal). He is a **cultist with an oily sheen to his eyes**, indicating true corruption, unlike Thalia.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia (physical_condition): ensorcelled; no oily sheen  \n- Thalia (mental_state): innocent; charmed status ended  \n- Thalia (loyalty): serves the Wolf (under influence), protector of city  \n- The Wolf (role): manipulator, cultist, corrupting influence  \n\nBottom line: Thalia was **played, not turned**\u2014a compromised ally, not a lost one.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
  ],
